1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,315
The trial run began on a crowded Monday.

2
00:00:02,315 --> 00:00:09,583
Three of them stood at the west gate with a hundred printed cards and asked every visitor a single question.

3
00:00:09,583 --> 00:00:17,865
The idea was to keep the test small, adapt it hourly, and describe the result without decorating it.

4
00:00:17,865 --> 00:00:23,998
“Yes, it is slow,” Maya admitted, reading the card again.

5
00:00:23,998 --> 00:00:43,321
“Those answers change nothing until we can show them to someone else, and your card is the only proof we have.” Their consent form was one sentence long, written for a stranger in a hurry, and the response rate was also better than anyone expected.

6
00:00:43,321 --> 00:00:48,640
By midnight the group had collected me a folder of handwritten answers.

7
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:55,013
A girl drew a clock going clockwise and wrote that the new route saved her four minutes.

8
00:00:55,013 --> 00:01:05,074
Maya laughed happily, hugged her, and said that such a small, meaningful result was the first real asset the project owned.

9
00:01:05,074 --> 00:01:09,878
A quick photo shoot followed, and no harm came of it.

10
00:01:09,878 --> 00:01:19,430
The novelty would fade, she warned her friends, but the loneliness of a student standing at a locked gate would not.

11
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:23,248
A collaborative mood was prevalent that week.

12
00:01:23,248 --> 00:01:36,264
Two of them went to a winery on the edge of the city to interview drivers, and the manager spoke openly about a knotty problem: the road was well off in summer and impassable in winter.

13
00:01:36,264 --> 00:01:48,539
Among the drivers, a dynasty of local growers had kept the same habit for a century, and no recyclable sign had ever been posted for the convenience of visitors.

14
00:01:48,539 --> 00:01:58,106
The valley was magnificent, and its magnificence made the failure easy to forgive; that was exactly the danger.

15
00:01:58,106 --> 00:02:04,979
Someone had tried to mislead the team with an imitative map copied from an imperialist survey.

16
00:02:04,979 --> 00:02:10,527
It was graphically beautiful and barely distinguishable from the real thing.

17
00:02:10,527 --> 00:02:18,734
Maya did not misunderstand the intention, but she refused to cherish a document that would pollute the record.

18
00:02:18,734 --> 00:02:27,061
A heartfelt apology arrived the next morning, and it was regrettable that it came after the delay rather than before it.

19
00:02:27,061 --> 00:02:33,079
She raised her hand at the meeting and asked for the source of every line.

20
00:02:33,079 --> 00:02:41,446
They agreed to reunite the two halves of the survey before the term review and to assess the feasibility of a permanent sign.

21
00:02:41,446 --> 00:02:52,293
Though the work accelerated quickly, they chose a leisurely evening to check every card anew and to congratulate the volunteers who had fled the rain with them.

22
00:02:52,293 --> 00:03:01,953
“Anything else,” Lin said, standing where the old ramp should have been, “can wait until tomorrow.”
